#!RuleTest
#test FDA-SE2308-A expect=violation domain=PC
#note "The half this R-5.25 split sibling owns (top-level-or board wave 2, group J): row 2 has neither VISITDY nor PCNOMDY populated - no day anchor - and fires ONCE, as one condition (the within-branch and-group stays whole; R-5.25 splits conditions, not leaves). Row 1 (PCELTM empty, VISITDY populated) is the parent FDA-SE2308's state and must NOT fire here - the discriminator, on the byte-identical dataset the parent's invalid fixture uses."
#library standard=sendig version=3-1
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=2 PCSEQ=2
dataset PC class=FINDINGS label="Pharmacokinetics Concentrations"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col PCSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col VISITDY type=Num  label="Planned Study Day of Visit"
col PCNOMDY type=Num  label="Nominal Study Day for Tabulations"
col PCELTM  type=Char label="Planned Elapsed Time from Time Point Ref"
---
S1 | PC | 001 | 1 | 3 | 1 |
S1 | PC | 001 | 2 | . | . | PT1H
S1 | PC | 001 | 3 | 3 | 1 | PT0H
